I find that difficult to imagine, in a codebase that dates to
the early eighties.  Architecture-independent binary file
formats were pretty much completely unheard-of back then.
Programmers of that era simply did not think that anyone
would some day need to take data from a 36-bit big-endian
system and use it on an 8-bit little-endian system, etc.
People were still getting used to the idea that plain text
files could be portable between architectures.


